ver, frustration often follows surprise when one's expectations or self-image are challenged. Given the context of seeking validation ("What about my muscles?"), frustration seems slightly more encompassing of the underlying issue than simple surprise.\n\n*Final Decision based on the strongest inference:* The man is seeking validation after his physique was dismissed. This points towards frustration at being overlooked.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
