came quiet.\n\n4.  **Conclusion:** The combination of "Easy now," "Wait," and the sudden, high-pitched reaction strongly suggests the speaker was surprised by an abrupt change in the horse's movement, most likely a sudden stop or refusal to move forward, which aligns best with option B.\n\n**Answer:**\n$$\boxed{B}$$
