d piece of music. If we interpret the question as: "Does the absence of the female speaker *guarantee* the appearance of a second piece of music?" the answer is clearly no, as there is no evidence of a second piece at all. If we interpret it as: "Will the music sequence continue?" we still lack evidence for continuation. Therefore, the safest answer based *only* on what is present is that the second piece will not appear because it is not demonstrated or implied to exist.\n\nAnswer: B\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{B}$
